        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "789ed63b-78e0-58cb-9745-8a7c97b408c0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Martin Degville, Richie Furay, Chris Hillman, J.D. Souther, Stephen Stills, Neil Young, Bruce Palmer, Dewey Martin, Jim Messina, Rusty Young, George Grantham, Randy Meisner, Tony James, Rusty Egan, Steve Strange, Boy George, Marilyn, Alice Temple, Perri Lister, Princess Julia, Philip Sallon, Carl Teper\n- Bands and Groups: Sigue Sigue Sputnik, Buffalo Springfield, Poco, Souther Hillman Furay Band, The Byrds, The Flying Burrito Brothers, Manassas, Longbranch Pennywhistle\n- Places: Walsall\n- Topics: country rock, pop music, Rock & Roll Hall of Fame, Blitz Kids\n\nFacts:\n- Richie Furay was born on May 9, 1944 and is an American singer, songwriter, and Rock & Roll Hall of Fame member.\n- Martin Degville was born on 27 January 1961 in Walsall.\n- In 1986, Sigue Sigue Sputnik had a worldwide hit single with \"Love Missile F1-11.\"\n- Martin Degville is the lead singer and co-songwriter of the UK pop band Sigue Sigue Sputnik.\n- Martin Degville later became the frontman of Tony James' Sigue Sigue Sputnik.\n- Sigue Sigue Sputnik had six other EMI single releases.\n- Richie Furay is best known for forming Buffalo Springfield with Stephen Stills, Neil Young, Bruce Palmer, and Dewey Martin.\n- Richie Furay is also best known for forming Poco with Jim Messina, Rusty Young, George Grantham, and Randy Meisner.\n- The Souther Hillman Furay Band was a country rock supergroup led by Richie Furay, Chris Hillman, and J.D. Souther.\n- Chris Hillman was associated with The Byrds, The Flying Burrito Brothers, and Manassas.\n- J.D. Souther was associated with Longbranch Pennywhistle and was a noted songwriter for Linda Ronstadt and the Eagles.\n- Attendees connected with the Blitz Kids scene included Rusty Egan, Steve Strange, Boy George, Marilyn, Alice Temple, Perri Lister, Princess Julia, Philip Sallon, Carl Teper, and Martin Degville.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
